        "id": "p41-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "32, 33, 33, 33, 33, 34, 35, 43, 48",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "IQR $=6$; lower fence $=24$; upper fence $=48$. No outliers.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}Q_1&=\\frac{33+33}{2}=33\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{35+43}{2}=39\\\\\\text{IQR}&=39-33=6\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=33-1.5\\times6=24\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=39+1.5\\times6=48\\end{aligned}$\n\nAll values lie between or on the fences. In particular, $48$ equals the upper fence, so it is not an outlier.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
